:paragraph -->\n<p>Once you\'ve hit <strong>Save</strong>, you\'re all set! You can now preview your draft theme to see the <strong>Sign Customizer</strong> in action and ensure everything is working perfectly before going live. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Need a hand?</strong> Check out the tutorial below for a step-by-step guide on enabling the <strong>Zepto Sign Customizer</strong>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:video {\"id\":113} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-video\"><video controls src=\"https://zcustomizer.app/docs/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/R-Enabling-Sign-Customizer-in-Themes.mp4\"></video></figure>\n<!-- /wp:video -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Thank you. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Enabling Sign Customizer in themes', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '106-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-02-16 06:43:46', '2026-02-16 06:43:46', '', 106, 'https://zcustomizer.app/docs/?p=115', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(116, 3, '2026-02-16 06:44:09', '2026-02-16 06:44:09', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>To get started, simply navigate to the <strong>Sign Customizer dashboard</strong> and click the <strong>Enable</strong> button to activate the app on your store.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":109,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://zcustomizer.app/docs/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/image-1024x449.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-109\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Once clicked, you’ll be automatically redirected to the <strong>App Embeds</strong> section of your live theme. Simply click <strong>Save</strong> in the top right corner, and you’re all set! </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":110,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://zcustomizer.app/docs/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/image-1-1024x477.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-110\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Want to test it out first? You can also enable the app on any <strong>draft theme</strong> by manually navigating to that theme\'s editor, selecting the <strong>App Embeds</strong> tab, and toggling the customizer on. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":111,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://zcustomizer.app/docs/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/image-2-1024x477.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-111\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":112,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://zcustomizer.app/docs/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/image-3-1024x477.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-112\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Once you\'ve hit <strong>Save</strong>, you\'re all set! You can now preview your draft theme to see the <strong>Sign Customizer</strong> in action and ensure everything is working perfectly before going live. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p> </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Need a hand?</strong> Check out the tutorial below for a step-by-step guide on enabling the <strong>Zepto Sign Customizer</strong>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:video {\"id\":113} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-video\"><video controls src=\"https://zcustomizer.app/docs/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/R-Enabling-Sign-Customizer-in-Themes.mp4\"></video></figure>\n<!-- /wp:video -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Thank you. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Enabling Sign Customizer in themes', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '106-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-02-16 06:44:09', '2026-02-16 06:44:09', '', 106, 'https://zcustomizer.app/docs/?p=116', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(117, 3, '2026-02-16 08:52:15', '2026-02-16 08:52:15', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Options for cost display: <br>      1. Create a new product method</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Create a new product method:</strong> <br>The initial method of pricing is called the \"Create a new product\" method, where we create a new product in your Shopify Products section, where the price will be the total pricing, including the base price and additional price. We use the final preview image as the feature image (media in Shopify). <br><br><img class=\"wp-image-123\" style=\"width: 800px;\" src=\"http://zcustomizer.app/docs/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Screenshot_2.png\" alt=\"\"><br><br>The products\' status will be set to \'Unlisted\' automatically, so they will not be visible on your website. <br><br><img class=\"wp-image-122\" style=\"width: 800px;\" src=\"http://zcustomizer.app/docs/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Screenshot_1.png\" alt=\"\"><br><br>If you want to delete the products that we are creating every time anyone clicks on the \" Add to cart\" button, you can simply enable the option \"Delete newly created product\" from the Settings of the app. Our app will automatically delete newly created products after a specified period. <br><br><img class=\"wp-image-118\" style=\"width: 800px;\" src=\"http://zcustomizer.app/docs/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Screenshot_11.png\" alt=\"\"><br>You can control the delete time by selecting the time. We recommend using the time for at least <strong>1 day</strong> to avoid issues later. If you set a 30-minute time window and someone adds a product to the cart but goes to the checkout page after 40 minutes, the product will not be added because it will be deleted after 30 minutes.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ol>\n<!-- /wp:list -->', 'How Options with Costs are displayed in the Cart &amp; Checkout', '', 'publish', 'open', 'closed', '', 'how-options-with-costs-are-displayed-in-the-cart-checkout', '', '', '2026-02-16 09:42:15', '2026-02-16 09:42:15', '', 0, 'https://zcustomizer.app/docs/?post_type=epkb_post_type_1&#038;p=117', 0, 'epkb_post_type_1', '', 0),
(118, 3, '2026-02-16 08:15:04', '2026-02-16 08:15:04', '', 'Screenshot_11', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', 'screenshot_11', '', '', '2026-02-16 08:15:04', '2026-02-16 08:15:04', '', 117, 'http://zcustomizer.app/docs/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Screenshot_11.png', 0, 'attachment', 'image/png', 0),
(119, 3, '2026-02-16 08:52:15', '2026-02-16 08:52:15', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Options for cost display: <br>      1. Create a new product method</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Create a new product method:</strong> <br>The initial method of pricing is called the \"Create a new product\" method, where we create a new product in your Shopify Products section, where the price will be the total pricing, including the base price and additional price. We use the final preview image as the feature image (media in Shopify). <br>If you want to delete the products that we are creating every time anyone clicks on the \" Add to cart\" button, you can simply enable the option \"Delete newly created product\" from the Settings of the app. Our app will automatically delete newly created products after a specified period. <br><br><img class=\"wp-image-118\" style=\"width: 800px;\" src=\"http://zcustomizer.app/docs/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Screenshot_11.png\" alt=\"\"><br><br>You can control the delete time by selecting the time. We recommend using the time for at least 1 day to avoid issues later. If you set a 30-minute time window and someone adds a product to the cart but goes to the checkout page after 40 minutes, the product will not be added because it will be deleted after 30 minutes. </li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ol>\n<!-- /wp:list -->', 'How Options with Costs are displayed in the Cart &amp; Checkout', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '117-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-02-16 08:52:15', '2026-02-16 08:52:15', '', 117, 'https://zcustomizer.app/docs/?p=119', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(120, 3, '2026-02-16 08:52:51', '2026-02-16 08:52:51', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Options for cost display: <br>      1. Create a new product method</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Create a new product method:</strong> <br>The initial method of pricing is called the \"Create a new product\" method, where we create a new product in your Shopify Products section, where the price will be the total pricing, including the base price and additional price. We use the final preview image as the feature image (media in Shopify). <br>If you want to delete the products that we are creating every time anyone clicks on the \" Add to cart\" button, you can simply enable the option \"Delete newly created product\" from the Settings of the app. Our app will automatically delete newly created products after a specified period. <br><br><img class=\"wp-image-118\" style=\"width: 800px;\" src=\"http://zcustomizer.app/docs/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Screenshot_11.png\" alt=\"\"><br>You can control the delete time by selecting the time. We recommend using the time for at least 1 day to avoid issues later. If you set a 30-minute time window and someone adds a product to the cart but goes to the checkout page after 40 minutes, the product will not be added because it will be deleted after 30 minutes. </li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ol>\n<!-- /wp:list -->', 'How Options with Costs are displayed in the Cart &amp; Checkout', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '117-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-02-16 08:52:51', '2026-02-16 08:52:51', '', 117, 'https://zcustomizer.app/docs/?p=120', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
